    {
      "id": "96a3e2e3-31f1-4f7d-bed5-8219c3e1dfeb",
      "name": "Workflow Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1392,
        -560
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 648,
        "height": 752,
        "content": "# Sync Calendly bookings to Airtable CRM and Slack\n\nAutomatically sync new Calendly bookings into an Airtable CRM and notify your team in Slack. This is useful for sales and operations teams that want every booked meeting captured without manual CRM updates.\n\n### How it works\n\n1. Calendly triggers the workflow when a new invitee books a meeting.\n2. Booking details are normalized and the Google Calendar event is matched so additional attendees can be added.\n3. The CRM is searched by email. Existing contacts are updated; new contacts are created.\n4. The workflow checks for an existing meeting using the Calendly event ID before creating a meeting record.\n5. A formatted Slack notification is sent with the booking details and meeting links.\n\n### Setup\n\n1. Connect Calendly, Google Calendar, Airtable, and Slack credentials.\n2. In `Template Configuration`, enter your Airtable base/table IDs, Google Calendar ID, Slack channel ID, and optional additional attendee emails.\n3. Create `Contacts` and `Meetings` tables in Airtable with the fields used by the CRM nodes.\n4. Select your Calendly user/event source in the trigger and activate the workflow.\n\n### Customization\n\nChange the Airtable field mappings, Slack notification, duplicate check, or additional calendar attendees to match your CRM."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
